<title>USA: Fluor Daniel to build Amoco plant.</title>
<headline>Fluor Daniel to build Amoco plant.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fluor Daniel said it was awarded a contract by Amoco Corp to design and construct a new metaxylene (MX) unit at its plant in Texas City, Texas.  Total project and Fluor Daniel contract values were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Metaxylene is a feedstock used to produce purified isophthalic acid (PIA), which is used to produce coatings, unsaturated polyesters, polyethylene terephthalate (PET) for container and fiber resins, engineering polymers, inks and adhesives.</p>
<p>The new unit will have a capacity of 100,000 tons per year.</p>
